<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the project code. The `MmsValue_newStructure` function does not handle the case where an element of a structure specification is `NULL`. It directly dereferences the element without checking if it's `NULL`.

A patch should be added to `MmsValue_newStructure` to check if `typeSpec->typeSpec.structure.elements[i]` is `NULL` before dereferencing it. If it is `NULL`, the function should probably handle it as an error, for example by returning `NULL` or a special error value.

Here is a suggested patch for `mms_value.c`:

```c
--- a/src/mms/iso_mms/common/mms_value.c
+++ b/src/mms/iso_mms/common/mms_value.c
@@ -1546,7 +1546,10 @@
for (i = 0; i < elementCount; i++) {
newStructureValue->value.structure.components[i] =
MmsValue_newDefaultValue(typeSpec->typeSpec.structure.elements[i]);
-
+        if (newStructureValue->value.structure.components[i] == NULL) {
+            /* TODO cleanup already allocated memory */
+            return NULL;
+        }
}

return (MmsValue*) newStructureValue;

```
</crash-analysis>

